---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { BRAND_NAME, BASE } from '../site';
import { PRACTICES, SERVICES } from '../data/services';
const faqs=[
 ['How much does a website cost?','Every project is quoted, because no two businesses need the same site. Tell us your budget in the form and we will tell you what fits, in writing, before you commit. What changes the price: number of pages, a store or app, and whether you need hosting and care after launch.'],
 ['How long does it take?','Most websites: 4–6 weeks from first call to launch. A focused build with ready content: 3 weeks. Larger builds: 8–12 weeks. Cloud, compliance and staffing engagements are scoped separately, with their own timelines in the written plan.'],
 ['Do you work outside Canada?','Yes — we are based in Canada and work worldwide, in your time zone.'],
 ['Who owns the website, the cloud account, and the data?','You do. Domain, website, cloud account, content and data — all in your accounts, in your name. No lock-in.'],
 ['What happens after launch?','Care plans cover hosting, updates, backups and small changes. Cancel anytime with 30 days notice. For cloud and compliance, ongoing management is a monthly service, quoted separately.'],
 ['I am not technical. Will I understand what is happening?','Yes — that is the point. You get one person to talk to, plain-English updates, and a site you can edit yourself. You never touch a server, a dashboard you do not understand, or a line of code. Technical detail is on every service page, below the plain-English version, for the people on your team who do want it.'],
 ['Do you certify us for HIPAA or PCI DSS?','No — and no vendor can. Your auditor certifies you, after reviewing evidence. We build the systems and prepare the evidence so you can pass. See Compliance Readiness.'],
];
---
<Base>
<section class="hero"><div class="container hero-grid">
<div>
<span class="kicker-chip">Managed-services company · Canada — working worldwide</span>
<h1 style="margin-top:20px">Your technology, <span class="grad">designed, built and run</span> by one team.</h1>
<p class="sub">One team that designs, builds, runs and staffs your technology — so your business keeps working, without you managing the technology. Web design, managed hosting, cloud, AI, compliance and talent: seven practices, one accountable team.</p>
<p class="tech">For non-technical owners: we do the technology, you run your business. For technical teams: the same team does managed hosting, cloud, Kubernetes &amp; OpenShift, AI and compliance readiness — with the detail on every service page.</p>
<div class="cta-row"><a class="btn" href={`${BASE}/contact`}>Book a strategy call →</a><a class="btn ghost" href={`${BASE}/practices`}>See the seven practices</a></div>
<p class="micro"><b>10–20 specialists</b> · Design, hosting, cloud, AI, compliance, consultancy &amp; talent · <b>Custom quote</b> — scoped before quoting</p>
</div>
<div class="mock" aria-label="What a homepage we build contains">
<div class="mock-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>yourbusiness.com</span></div>
<div class="mock-body">
<div class="m-h"></div>
<div class="m-p"></div><div class="m-p short"></div>
<span class="mock-btn">Get a quote →</span>
<div class="mock-stats">
<div><b>&lt;1.5s</b><span>Load-time target, every site</span></div>
<div><b>100%</b><span>Mobile-first, responsive</span></div>
<div><b>4–6 wks</b><span>Typical website launch</span></div>
<div><b>You own it</b><span>Domain, site &amp; data</span></div>
</div>
<p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--soft);margin:12px 0 0">An example homepage layout — the sections a homepage we build contains. Not a client site.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div></section>

<section class="answer tight"><div class="container"><div class="answer-grid">
<div class="answer-card"><b>What we do</b><span>Design, build and run your technology — websites, hosting, cloud, AI, compliance and talent.</span></div>
<div class="answer-card"><b>Who it's for</b><span>Small businesses, growing stores, and technical teams — in Canada and worldwide.</span></div>
<div class="answer-card"><b>What you get</b><span>A fast site you own, hosting that is watched, cloud that is documented, and people you can call.</span></div>
<div class="answer-card"><b>What it costs</b><span>Custom quote, scoped before quoting. Tell us your budget — we tell you what fits, before you commit.</span></div>
<div class="answer-card"><b>What happens next</b><span>1 · Book a strategy call → 2 · We scope it in writing → 3 · You decide.</span></div>
</div></div></section>

<section><div class="container">
<div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">What do you need first?</p><h2>Start where your problem is.</h2><p class="lead">Three doors, one team behind all of them. Pick the one that matches your problem — you can add the others later, and none requires the others.</p></div>
<div class="grid3">
<div class="card silo"><span class="tag">New website, store or app</span><h3>I need a website that works</h3><p class="plain">A website, store or app your customers love — and you can edit yourself.</p><a href={`${BASE}/services/website-services`}>Website Services →</a></div>
<div class="card silo"><span class="tag">Hosting that just works</span><h3>My site must stay up</h3><p class="plain">Managed WordPress, VPS and dedicated — set up, secured, backed up and watched.</p><a href={`${BASE}/services/managed-hosting`}>Managed Hosting →</a></div>
<div class="card silo"><span class="tag">Cloud, compliance or talent</span><h3>We need specialists</h3><p class="plain">Cloud, containers, AI, compliance readiness, consultancy and staffing — by specialists.</p><a href={`${BASE}/services/professional-services`}>Professional Services →</a></div>
</div></div></section>

<section style="background:var(--bg)"><div class="container">
<div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">Seven practices</p><h2>Seven practices. Each one stands alone.</h2><p class="lead">Design is one of seven — not the headline, not a footnote. Every practice has its own page, its own services, and its own proof line.</p></div>
<div class="grid3"><div class="card silo"><h3>Web Design & Experience</h3><p class="plain">Websites, stores and apps people love to use — and you can edit yourself.</p><p class="tech">Built on WordPress — 38.6% of the web (W3Techs, Nov 2026).</p><a href={BASE + "/practices/web-design-experience"}>Explore Web Design & Experience →</a></div>
<div class="card silo"><h3>Managed Hosting</h3><p class="plain">Hosting that just works — set up, secured, backed up and watched.</p><p class="tech">Daily backups, SSL and monitoring. You never touch a server.</p><a href={BASE + "/practices/managed-hosting"}>Explore Managed Hosting →</a></div>
<div class="card silo"><h3>Cloud & Containers</h3><p class="plain">Cloud, Kubernetes and OpenShift, run for you.</p><p class="tech">Managed clusters, upgrades and monitoring included.</p><a href={BASE + "/practices/cloud-containers"}>Explore Cloud & Containers →</a></div>
<div class="card silo"><h3>AI</h3><p class="plain">Practical AI in the tools you already use.</p><p class="tech">Data boundaries checked first. No hype, no data leaks.</p><a href={BASE + "/practices/ai"}>Explore AI →</a></div>
<div class="card silo"><h3>Compliance Readiness</h3><p class="plain">Cloud set up to meet HIPAA, PCI DSS and SOC 2 — readiness, not certification.</p><p class="tech">Gap review + landing zone + audit evidence pack.</p><a href={BASE + "/practices/compliance-readiness"}>Explore Compliance Readiness →</a></div>
<div class="card silo"><h3>Consultancy</h3><p class="plain">A clear plan before you spend.</p><p class="tech">Architecture, vendors and roadmap, in writing.</p><a href={BASE + "/practices/consultancy"}>Explore Consultancy →</a></div>
<div class="card silo"><h3>Staffing & Talent</h3><p class="plain">Specialists matched in days, embedded in your team.</p><p class="tech">Project-based. No long contract, no hiring overhead.</p><a href={BASE + "/practices/staffing-talent"}>Explore Staffing & Talent →</a></div>
</div>
<div style="overflow-x:auto;margin-top:28px"><table class="compare">
<tr><th>Practice</th><th>What it covers</th><th>Ongoing or project?</th><th>Who it is for</th></tr>
<tr><td>Web Design &amp; Experience</td><td>Websites, UX, builder, apps, stores</td><td>Project, then Care</td><td>Businesses that need a website</td></tr>
<tr><td>Managed Hosting</td><td>WordPress, VPS, dedicated</td><td>Ongoing, monthly</td><td>Sites that must stay up</td></tr>
<tr><td>Cloud &amp; Containers</td><td>Cloud, Kubernetes, OpenShift, containers</td><td>Project, then ongoing</td><td>Teams running real infrastructure</td></tr>
<tr><td>AI</td><td>AI consulting, chat, content, automation</td><td>Project, then rollout</td><td>Teams with repetitive work to automate</td></tr>
<tr><td>Compliance Readiness</td><td>HIPAA / PCI DSS / SOC 2 readiness</td><td>Project, then ongoing</td><td>Regulated businesses preparing for audit</td></tr>
<tr><td>Consultancy</td><td>Architecture, vendors, roadmap</td><td>Project</td><td>Businesses about to spend on technology</td></tr>
<tr><td>Staffing &amp; Talent</td><td>Designers, developers, vetted talent</td><td>Per sprint / per project</td><td>Teams with more work than people</td></tr>
</table></div>
</div></section>

<section><div class="container">
<div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">Three different things</p><h2>Ongoing services, projects, and staffing are not the same thing.</h2><p class="lead">Providers blur them together, and it makes proposals hard to compare. They are billed differently, they start and stop differently, and you can buy any one without the others.</p></div>
<div class="grid3">
<div class="card"><h3>Ongoing services</h3><p>Monthly. Somebody is responsible on a Tuesday afternoon when nothing is on fire — hosting, monitoring, updates, backups. That is most of what you are actually paying for.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>One-off projects</h3><p>A beginning and an end. A website, a migration, a landing zone, a compliance review. Scoped and priced as a project, and it does not require you to hand over your day-to-day technology.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Staffing</h3><p>A person, for a fixed period. A designer, a developer, a cloud engineer — embedded in your team, in your tools, then gone, with documentation left behind.</p></div>
</div>
<p style="margin-top:20px"><strong>We scope before we quote.</strong> A number produced without seeing your business is a guess you would end up budgeting against.</p>
</div></section>

<section style="background:var(--bg)"><div class="container">
<div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">How it works</p><h2>From first call to launch in 4–6 weeks.</h2><p class="lead">Five steps. At every step you know what you do, and what you get.</p></div>
<div class="steps">
<div class="step"><b>01</b><h3>Discover</h3><p>Week 1 — we learn your business, your customers and your goals.</p><div class="you"><b>You do:</b> one 45-min call + a short brief.</div></div>
<div class="step"><b>02</b><h3>Design</h3><p>Weeks 2–3 — wireframes, then visual design. You see it on desktop and phone.</p><div class="you"><b>You do:</b> 2 rounds of feedback.</div></div>
<div class="step"><b>03</b><h3>Build</h3><p>Weeks 3–5 — design becomes a fast, working site. SEO, speed and accessibility built in.</p><div class="you"><b>You do:</b> approve content.</div></div>
<div class="step"><b>04</b><h3>Launch</h3><p>Week 5–6 — every page tested, hosting and analytics set up, then live.</p><div class="you"><b>You do:</b> nothing — we handle it.</div></div>
<div class="step"><b>05</b><h3>Care</h3><p>Ongoing — hosting, updates, backups and small changes, every month.</p><div class="you"><b>You do:</b> run your business.</div></div>
</div>
<p style="margin-top:20px"><a href={`${BASE}/process`}>See the full process →</a></p></div></section>

<section><div class="container">
<div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">What it costs</p><h2>Custom quote — and honest about what changes it.</h2><p class="lead">We don't publish a price we haven't settled, and we don't hide the price behind a sales call. These are the things that move the quote — tell us your budget, and we'll tell you what fits, in writing, before you commit.</p></div>
<div class="cost">
<table>
<tr><th>What changes the price</th><th>How</th></tr>
<tr><td>Number of pages</td><td>More pages, more design and content work</td></tr>
<tr><td>Online store</td><td>Products, payments, shipping and tax setup</td></tr>
<tr><td>Mobile app</td><td>iOS + Android publishing, logins, payments</td></tr>
<tr><td>Hosting &amp; care</td><td>Managed hosting, updates, backups, small changes</td></tr>
<tr><td>Cloud / compliance</td><td>Scoped per project — quoted after a short review</td></tr>
</table>
<div class="note blue"><strong>Your budget is the starting point, not a secret.</strong><br/>Put your budget in the form — Under $5k, $5–15k, $15–50k, $50k+, or Not sure — and we'll reply within 1 business day with what fits. If we can't help, we'll say so and point you to what can.</div>
</div></div></section>

<section style="background:var(--bg)"><div class="container">
<div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">Work</p><h2>Example scopes — what a project like yours looks like.</h2><p class="lead">Detailed, typical projects of each type — problem, what was built, stack, timeline and outcome. They are example scopes, not named client projects. Real client stories land here as they ship, with real names and real numbers.</p></div>
<div class="grid3">
<div class="work-card"><div class="art"><span class="pill">Example scope · Website</span><b>Small business website</b></div><div class="body"><p><strong>Problem:</strong> a service business that lived on phone calls, with a website that did not explain what it did or let anyone book.</p><a href={`${BASE}/work/small-business-website`}>Read the full example scope →</a></div></div>
<div class="work-card"><div class="art" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0E3A5C,var(--accent))"><span class="pill">Example scope · Store</span><b>Online store, rebuilt</b></div><div class="body"><p><strong>Problem:</strong> a small shop whose checkout was losing sales on phones.</p><a href={`${BASE}/work/online-store`}>Read the full example scope →</a></div></div>
<div class="work-card"><div class="art" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#2A1B6E,#14305E)"><span class="pill">Example scope · Hosting</span><b>Managed WordPress migration</b></div><div class="body"><p><strong>Problem:</strong> a WordPress site that kept breaking, with backups that had never been tested.</p><a href={`${BASE}/work/wordpress-migration`}>Read the full example scope →</a></div></div>
</div>
<p style="margin-top:20px"><a href={`${BASE}/work`}>See all example scopes →</a></p></div></section>

<section><div class="container">
<div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">What we believe</p><h2>One team, start to finish.</h2></div>
<div class="why">
<div class="card"><h3>No hand-offs</h3><p>Design, build, hosting and care — one team, no messages lost between vendors. You talk to the people doing the work.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Fast by default</h3><p>Every site is built to load in under 1.5 seconds. Speed is a feature, not an add-on — and it is measured, not claimed.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>You own everything</h3><p>Your domain, your site, your data, your cloud account. No lock-in, ever — your accounts, in your name.</p></div>
</div>
<blockquote style="font-size:24px;color:var(--navy);border-left:4px solid var(--accent);padding-left:22px;max-width:760px;margin-top:40px">“We build the technology we'd want to run ourselves — fast, clear, and honest.”<footer style="font-size:15px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:10px">— The {BRAND_NAME} team, on what we believe</footer></blockquote>
</div></section>

<section style="background:var(--bg)"><div class="container faq"><div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p><h2>Before you ask.</h2></div>
{faqs.map(f=><details><summary>{f[0]}</summary><p style="margin-top:10px">{f[1]}</p></details>)}
</div></section>
</Base>
